54283.sol:
The resistance of conductor
or $\quad R \propto \frac{l}{r^2}R=\frac{\rho l}{A}=\frac{\rho l}{\pi r^2}\begin{aligned}
\therefore \quad \frac{R_1}{R_2} & =\frac{l_1}{l_2} \times \frac{r_2^2}{r_1^2} \\
& =\frac{2}{1} \times\left(\frac{2}{1}\right)^2=\frac{8}{1}
\end{aligned}$<br/>Thermal potentials between the ends of the rods are same. So, heat conducted per second
$\begin{aligned}
& H=\frac{Q}{t} \propto \frac{1}{R} \\
\therefore & \frac{H_1}{H_2}=\frac{R_2}{R_1}=\frac{1}{8}=1: 8
\end{aligned}$

